1
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:13,171
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,389 --> 00:00:15,355
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:18,973
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:18,998 --> 00:00:24,489
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

5
00:00:25,485 --> 00:00:28,824
We all know Uhud(أحَد), to be a defeat,

6
00:00:30,709 --> 00:00:34,754
but the amazing thing is that Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) thinks otherwise.

7
00:00:35,855 --> 00:00:38,572
Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) says that it is a victory for the Muslims.

8
00:00:39,876 --> 00:00:41,960
The reason why it's a victory for the Muslims is

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,627
because it's a gold mine of lessons.

10
00:00:45,094 --> 00:00:52,059
It's a treasure trove, Ibbar(عِبَّرْ), historical lessons that could be learned

11
00:00:52,626 --> 00:00:54,321
from this amazing event.

12
00:00:55,399 --> 00:01:00,537
So, In Sha Allah Ta'ala(ان شاءالله تعالى) we will devote this entire session, to lessons from the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

13
00:01:02,043 --> 00:01:02,922
Number one,

14
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:08,360
and by the way, these lessons we're going to be driving, mostly from Qur'an from Surat Al-Imran(سورة العمران).

15
00:01:08,863 --> 00:01:10,900
And again to refresh your memories

16
00:01:11,348 --> 00:01:14,620
Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال) was revealed after the Battle of Badr(بدر)

17
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:19,223
and Surat Al-Imran(سورة العمران) was revealed after the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

18
00:01:19,712 --> 00:01:24,477
So these two Su'ar(سُوَر) are dealing with these two great battles.

19
00:01:25,401 --> 00:01:28,976
Number one, study history.

20
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:31,272
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

21
00:01:31,527 --> 00:01:36,934
قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ سُنَنٌ فَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ

22
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:44,720
 فَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ۝

23
00:01:45,287 --> 00:01:49,631
Similar conditions as yours have passed on before.

24
00:01:50,292 --> 00:01:53,536
So, proceed throughout the earth and observe,

25
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:56,360
how was the end of those, who denied.

26
00:01:57,343 --> 00:02:01,026
Go and travel and see what happened to the nation's before

27
00:02:01,138 --> 00:02:03,585
 learn history, study the lessons,

28
00:02:04,984 --> 00:02:07,997
look at the conflict between good and evil and the outcome of it.

29
00:02:09,892 --> 00:02:14,093
This Qur'an is a clear statement to all the people

30
00:02:14,236 --> 00:02:18,109
 and a guidance and instruction for those conscious of Allah.

31
00:02:19,263 --> 00:02:22,780
Now, we cannot benefit from history.

32
00:02:23,467 --> 00:02:28,701
If we don't believe in the authenticity of the rule of cause and effect.

33
00:02:29,821 --> 00:02:33,890
We have to believe that causes do lead to certain results.

34
00:02:34,694 --> 00:02:37,495
If that wasn't the case, then there's no benefit in studying history.

35
00:02:37,556 --> 00:02:39,892
Because when we study history, what we're looking at,

36
00:02:40,461 --> 00:02:45,157
are the causes that lead to certain results.

37
00:02:45,781 --> 00:02:48,093
So, the cause effect, rule has to be correct.

38
00:02:48,729 --> 00:02:51,720
So, we believe if you do this, the outcome would be that,

39
00:02:52,301 --> 00:02:54,213
this is how we benefit from history.

40
00:02:54,580 --> 00:03:00,437
So, we look at the believers of the early nations and we try to emulate them.

41
00:03:00,825 --> 00:03:06,823
And we look at the disbelievers of the former nations and we try to avoid their practices.

42
00:03:07,251 --> 00:03:10,851
That is how we can benefit from history because this is not storytelling.

43
00:03:11,668 --> 00:03:15,273
Allah is not telling us to study history, to entertain ourselves,

44
00:03:15,353 --> 00:03:18,393
 Allah is telling us to study history to learn the lessons.

45
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:21,135
لَقَدْ كَانَ فِي قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ

46
00:03:21,393 --> 00:03:24,488
You have lessons to learn from their stories.

47
00:03:25,907 --> 00:03:28,813
So, this is the first thing, is to study history.

48
00:03:29,148 --> 00:03:30,123
And that's what we're doing here.

49
00:03:30,163 --> 00:03:35,935
We're talking about the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and this is the greatest part of history.

50
00:03:36,055 --> 00:03:38,163
We're studying the life of the final prophet,

51
00:03:38,556 --> 00:03:41,733
the one whose message will carry on until the Day of Judgment,

52
00:03:41,906 --> 00:03:47,573
no other prophet had the blessing of being the Nabi(نبي) to all mankind

53
00:03:47,827 --> 00:03:52,173
and to have his message carry on until the Day of Judgment except Muhammadﷺ.

54
00:03:52,529 --> 00:04:00,377
وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ إِلَّا رَحْمَةً لِلْعَالَمِينَ۝

55
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:03,500
We have sent you as mercy to all mankind.

56
00:04:04,756 --> 00:04:05,715
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

57
00:04:05,795 --> 00:04:10,007
وَكَانَ نَبِيُّ بَعْثَه’ اِلَى قَوْمِه خَاصَهْ وَبُعِثْتُ اِلَى النَّاسِ عَامَّهْ

58
00:04:10,227 --> 00:04:13,888
Every prophet before me, was sent to his specific nation

59
00:04:14,049 --> 00:04:15,887
while I am sent to all mankind.

60
00:04:16,869 --> 00:04:18,107
The second lesson,

61
00:04:18,385 --> 00:04:19,726
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

62
00:04:19,915 --> 00:04:29,152
وَلَا تَهِنُوا وَلَا تَحْزَنُوا وَأَنْتُمُ الْأَعْلَوْنَ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ۝

63
00:04:29,722 --> 00:04:33,129
So, do not weaken and do not grieve,

64
00:04:33,501 --> 00:04:36,679
and you are superior, if you are true believers.

65
00:04:36,961 --> 00:04:38,242
When was this revealed?

66
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,632
Let's look at the context, this was revealed after the defeat of Uhud(أحَد).

67
00:04:43,715 --> 00:04:45,247
When the spirits were low,

68
00:04:46,098 --> 00:04:48,096
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling them;

69
00:04:48,921 --> 00:04:52,257
Do not weaken and do not grieve,

70
00:04:53,023 --> 00:04:54,515
when you are superior.

71
00:04:55,425 --> 00:04:58,269
You are superior, even though you lost.

72
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,716
So, the Muslims should never forget this.

73
00:05:01,228 --> 00:05:05,497
You are superior to every other nation, no matter what.

74
00:05:06,522 --> 00:05:11,311
Even if the Ummah(امة) is defeated, even if the Ummah(امة) is weak, even if it is oppressed.

75
00:05:11,691 --> 00:05:14,970
This Ummah(امة) is still the best Ummah(امة) and the Ayaah(آية) that says:

76
00:05:15,013 --> 00:05:17,089
كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ

77
00:05:17,129 --> 00:05:18,849
Is an Ayaah(آية) in Surat Al-Imran(سورة العمران),

78
00:05:19,106 --> 00:05:21,144
which was revealed after the defeat of Uhud(أحَد).

79
00:05:22,102 --> 00:05:24,479
You were the best nation brought forth to mankind.

80
00:05:24,776 --> 00:05:26,397
This Ayaah(آية) didn't come after Badr(بدر),

81
00:05:26,762 --> 00:05:28,128
it didn't come after Fatiha Makkah(فتح مكه),

82
00:05:28,323 --> 00:05:32,748
it didn't come when the Islamic Empire was covering two thirds of Earth.

83
00:05:33,064 --> 00:05:37,181
This was revealed after the worst defeat that the Muslims suffered in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

84
00:05:37,221 --> 00:05:38,694
and that's the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

85
00:05:39,369 --> 00:05:42,958
So, Allah is telling them remember who you are, Keep that in mind.

86
00:05:44,425 --> 00:05:45,662
The third lesson

87
00:05:45,702 --> 00:05:55,883
and actually, we have here Seven lessons bundled together in verses 140, 143

88
00:05:56,145 --> 00:05:58,862
so we'll go over them all by reciting the Ayaah(آية).

89
00:06:00,269 --> 00:06:03,273
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

90
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:10,092
إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ ۚ

91
00:06:10,385 --> 00:06:15,489
وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ

92
00:06:15,743 --> 00:06:24,226
وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَاءَ ۗ

93
00:06:24,456 --> 00:06:28,713
وَاللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

94
00:06:29,025 --> 00:06:37,591
 وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

95
00:06:38,046 --> 00:06:50,684
أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ۝

96
00:06:51,022 --> 00:07:03,721
 وَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَلْقَوْهُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُمُوهُ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ۝

97
00:07:04,288 --> 00:07:06,211
If a wound should touch you,

98
00:07:06,991 --> 00:07:10,876
there has already, touched the opposing people a wound similar to it.

99
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:16,742
And these days of varying conditions we alternate among the people,

100
00:07:17,259 --> 00:07:20,874
so that Allah may make evident those who believe

101
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:24,279
and may take himself from among you Shuhadaa(شهدآء).

102
00:07:24,814 --> 00:07:27,006
And Allah does not like the wrongdoers.

103
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:31,923
And that Allah may purify the believers through trials

104
00:07:32,316 --> 00:07:34,423
and destroy the disbelievers.

105
00:07:35,032 --> 00:07:40,281
Or do you think that you would enter Paradise, while Allah has not yet made evident,

106
00:07:40,516 --> 00:07:42,685
those of you, who fight in His cause,

107
00:07:43,033 --> 00:07:45,732
and made evident those who are steadfast

108
00:07:46,756 --> 00:07:49,055
and you had certainly wished for death

109
00:07:49,471 --> 00:07:51,199
before you encountered it.

110
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:55,489
And you have now seen it before you, while you are looking on.

111
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:59,969
So, there are seven lessons in these four verses.

112
00:08:00,344 --> 00:08:03,518
Number one, if a wound should touch you,

113
00:08:03,607 --> 00:08:07,994
 there has already touched the opposing people a wound similar to it.

114
00:08:08,407 --> 00:08:09,496
 What does this indicate?

115
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,979
What does Allah telling us?

116
00:08:12,225 --> 00:08:14,048
Again, if a wound should touch you,

117
00:08:14,623 --> 00:08:18,672
there has already touched the opposing people a wound similar to it.

118
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:23,795
Because Muslims now have lost the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

119
00:08:24,025 --> 00:08:25,727
And again, the spirits were low

120
00:08:26,111 --> 00:08:28,418
and this is a defeated army.

121
00:08:28,555 --> 00:08:32,177
 And we know how weak the morale is with a defeated army.

122
00:08:32,507 --> 00:08:35,281
Things are bleak and depressed.

123
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,117
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling them;

124
00:08:38,981 --> 00:08:44,477
that, what happened to you has happened to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

125
00:08:45,283 --> 00:08:48,568
If you are suffering wounds now, they suffered wounds a year ago.

126
00:08:49,053 --> 00:08:53,433
If you are suffering defeat now, they suffered the same defeat a year ago.

127
00:08:53,901 --> 00:08:57,526
Now if that did not prevent them from carrying on the fight,

128
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,407
and coming to meet you in Uhud(أحَد),

129
00:08:59,645 --> 00:09:03,113
these wounds should not stop you from carrying on the fight.

130
00:09:03,482 --> 00:09:05,930
So, the Muffassireen(مفسرين) say, what is meant here

131
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:09,514
is that what happened to you is happening to them

132
00:09:09,824 --> 00:09:13,190
and since you are expecting from Allah what they don't expect

133
00:09:13,606 --> 00:09:15,578
and that is Jannah(جنة) and the rewards from Him.

134
00:09:15,947 --> 00:09:18,683
You should carry on the fight and you should never give up,

135
00:09:18,708 --> 00:09:21,093
and you should never lay down your arms.

136
00:09:21,597 --> 00:09:23,036
You should hit the ground running.

137
00:09:23,544 --> 00:09:27,317
Whatever happened to you should not let you give up,

138
00:09:28,194 --> 00:09:30,356
and should not defeat your souls.

139
00:09:30,769 --> 00:09:32,572
The spirits must remain high.

140
00:09:33,975 --> 00:09:37,213
إِنْ يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِثْلُهُ ۚ

141
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,173
So be patient.

142
00:09:39,330 --> 00:09:41,342
You wounded, be patient.

143
00:09:42,168 --> 00:09:44,108
Some of you are killed, be patient,

144
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,622
you lost, be patient,

145
00:09:47,646 --> 00:09:49,709
have perseverance, be steadfast.

146
00:09:50,864 --> 00:09:51,693
Number two,

147
00:09:52,106 --> 00:09:55,412
 وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ

148
00:09:56,071 --> 00:10:01,047
And these days of varying conditions, we alternate among the people.

149
00:10:01,362 --> 00:10:04,185
One day you win, the next day you lose.

150
00:10:04,225 --> 00:10:06,644
That's how it is, in this life.

151
00:10:07,066 --> 00:10:08,920
It's the yin and the yang of history.

152
00:10:10,008 --> 00:10:13,279
It's not all on one condition, you're not going to always win.

153
00:10:13,705 --> 00:10:15,671
And also you're not going to always lose.

154
00:10:16,057 --> 00:10:18,656
Now let's look at what Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) said about this.

155
00:10:19,695 --> 00:10:20,516
He said;

156
00:10:20,702 --> 00:10:29,544
اَنَّ حِكْمَة الله وَ سُنَّتَه’ فِيْ رُسُلِهِ وَاَتْبَاعِهِمْ جَرَتْ بِاَنْ يُدَالُوا مَرَّة وَ يُدَالُوا عَلَيْهِمْ اُخْرَى،

157
00:10:29,949 --> 00:10:32,187
لَكِنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهُمُ الْعَاقِبَهْ

158
00:10:32,656 --> 00:10:35,671
He said, it was the wisdom of Allah

159
00:10:35,934 --> 00:10:43,565
and His way with His prophets and their followers that they would once win and once lose,

160
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:46,098
but in the end, they are the victorious.

161
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:49,505
So, the end result is that Islam will win.

162
00:10:49,718 --> 00:10:52,940
However, until we reach to that stage,

163
00:10:53,269 --> 00:10:56,050
it's going to be a win and lose situation.

164
00:10:56,776 --> 00:10:58,705
You win once and you lose the next.

165
00:10:59,158 --> 00:10:59,827
And then he said;

166
00:10:59,962 --> 00:11:07,567
فَاِنَّهُمْ لَوْ اِنْتَصَرُوْدَآئِمًا دَخَلَ مَعَه’اَلْمُؤمِنُوْنَ وَغَيْرَهُمْ وَلَمْ يَتَمَيَّزْ اَلصَّادِقْ مِنْ غَيْرَه

167
00:11:07,983 --> 00:11:13,947
He said, If the believers always win, then others will join them.

168
00:11:14,534 --> 00:11:18,889
And then it wouldn't be clear, who are the believers and who are not.

169
00:11:19,229 --> 00:11:22,782
So, to distinguish the believers from the non believers

170
00:11:22,862 --> 00:11:26,560
there must be this alternating conditions of winning and losing

171
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,560
because if the Muslims are winning all the time,

172
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:33,195
then everybody is gonna recognize that this is the winning party and everybody's gonna join.

173
00:11:33,850 --> 00:11:38,195
And some of them would only join for worldly reasons, not for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

174
00:11:38,235 --> 00:11:41,545
So, this is the Hikmah(حكمه) behind winning and losing.

175
00:11:41,985 --> 00:11:42,896
And then he says,

176
00:11:42,987 --> 00:11:47,978
وَلَوْ اِنْتَصِرَ عَلَيْهِمْ دَآئِمًا لَمْ يَحْصِلِ الْمَقْصُوْدْ مِنَّ الْبِعْثَة وَالرِّسَالَهْ

177
00:11:48,364 --> 00:11:50,583
And if the Muslims are always losing then,

178
00:11:50,737 --> 00:11:54,586
the objective of sending the prophets would not be fulfilled,

179
00:11:54,626 --> 00:12:00,916
and that is for this religion to spread, and to win, converts and to rule the earth.

180
00:12:01,427 --> 00:12:05,179
So, it is not appropriate for the believers to always win,

181
00:12:05,204 --> 00:12:07,671
and it's not also appropriate for them to always lose.

182
00:12:07,979 --> 00:12:09,401
It's a mixture of both.

183
00:12:09,647 --> 00:12:13,489
And this is for the conditions of the test to be appropriate.

184
00:12:14,021 --> 00:12:20,305
So, the losing phases separate the true believers from the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

185
00:12:20,513 --> 00:12:24,378
And the winning phases are the ones that spread the religion.

186
00:12:24,698 --> 00:12:27,620
So, you have both objectives fulfilled.

187
00:12:28,884 --> 00:12:30,557
The third lesson,

188
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:31,895
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

189
00:12:31,935 --> 00:12:34,864
وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا

190
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:38,578
So, that Allah may make evident, those who believe

191
00:12:39,537 --> 00:12:44,854
and as we mentioned before, the true test of Eeman(ايمان) is Jihad(جهاد) Feesabeel Lillah(في سبيل الله).

192
00:12:45,328 --> 00:12:47,338
That is the true test of men.

193
00:12:47,977 --> 00:12:50,345
That is where the truth comes out.

194
00:12:50,817 --> 00:12:53,253
And that is where the fakeness shows.

195
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:57,737
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that what happened to you in Uhud(أحَد)

196
00:12:58,130 --> 00:13:03,157
is to separate the believers from the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

197
00:13:04,172 --> 00:13:05,140
The fourth lesson,

198
00:13:05,434 --> 00:13:08,981
وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنْكُمْ شُهَدَاءَ

199
00:13:09,363 --> 00:13:15,179
And that Allah may take to himself from among you, Shuhadaa(شهدآء).

200
00:13:15,725 --> 00:13:17,059
Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) says,

201
00:13:17,332 --> 00:13:21,681
اِنَّ اشَّهَادَتَ عِنْدَه’ مِنْ اَعْلَى مَرَاتِ بِاَوْلِيَآْءِ

202
00:13:22,251 --> 00:13:25,559
وَشُّهَدَآءُهُمْ خَوَاصُه’ وَالْمٌقَرَّبُوْنَ عَلَيْه

203
00:13:26,042 --> 00:13:34,658
Shahadah(شهادة), martyrdom is among the highest status in the eyes of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

204
00:13:34,756 --> 00:13:38,177
it comes right after the Anbiyaa(أنبياء) and the Siddiqeen(صديقين).

205
00:13:38,427 --> 00:13:38,795
And he said;

206
00:13:38,835 --> 00:13:41,803
وَشُّهَدَآءُهُمْ خَوَاصُه’ وَالْمٌقَرَّبُوْنَ إلَيْه

207
00:13:42,019 --> 00:13:46,125
And the martyrs are the ones, whom Allah draws closer to Him.

208
00:13:46,545 --> 00:13:49,887
These are the ones, whom Allahعَزّوجَلّ loves and brings close to Him.

209
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:56,904
وَلَا سَبِيْلَ اِلَى نَيْلِ هَذِهِ الدَّرَجَة اِلَّا بِتَقْدِيْرِ الْاَسْبَابِ الْمُفْضِيَّةِ اِلَيْهَا مِنْ تَسْلِيْط الْعَدُّوّْ

210
00:13:57,212 --> 00:14:05,496
And how can there be Shuhadaa(شهدآء), if Allahعَزّوجَلّ doesn't allow the enemy to kill some of the Muslims.

211
00:14:06,230 --> 00:14:08,238
So, if Shahadah(شهادة) is such a high status?

212
00:14:08,409 --> 00:14:10,564
How are some people going to achieve it?

213
00:14:10,804 --> 00:14:14,968
The only way for them to achieve it, is through the hands of the enemy.

214
00:14:15,266 --> 00:14:18,071
And this is one of the wisdoms of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

215
00:14:18,345 --> 00:14:22,035
Allahعَزّوجَلّ took to himself 70 shuhadaa(شهدآء).

216
00:14:23,849 --> 00:14:24,840
Number five,

217
00:14:25,355 --> 00:14:30,114
وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَمْحَقَ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

218
00:14:30,538 --> 00:14:38,487
And that Allah may purify the believers through trials and destroy the disbelievers.

219
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:41,336
 So, number one,

220
00:14:41,565 --> 00:14:43,664
وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا

221
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,952
So, that Allah may purify the believers.

222
00:14:47,238 --> 00:14:49,643
Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) has some interesting words, he said;

223
00:14:49,908 --> 00:14:54,695
Allahعَزّوجَلّ loves some of His servants so much,

224
00:14:55,545 --> 00:14:58,833
he reserves for them high places in Jannah(جنة).

225
00:14:59,568 --> 00:15:03,275
So, you have this high place, high level in Jannah(جنة)

226
00:15:03,542 --> 00:15:07,786
reserved for this certain servant of Allah, because Allah loves him.

227
00:15:08,507 --> 00:15:15,517
However, the deeds of this servant are not sufficient enough to take him up to that level.

228
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:17,739
So, how could he achieve it?

229
00:15:18,343 --> 00:15:24,198
It is by Allah making him, go through trials in Duniyah(دنيا) suffering hardship, pain,

230
00:15:24,844 --> 00:15:30,368
and that is how he can climb up to his high reserve status in paradise.

231
00:15:31,607 --> 00:15:34,899
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ loved some of these Sahabah(صحابه) so much,

232
00:15:35,437 --> 00:15:40,188
but because their deeds are not sufficient to take them up to that level reserved for them in Jannah(جنة),

233
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:44,243
Allahعَزّوجَلّ made them go through the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) and suffer the pain

234
00:15:44,477 --> 00:15:47,370
and hardship and injury and defeat

235
00:15:48,512 --> 00:15:53,877
and suffer the sad feelings of hearing the false news that Rasool Allah ﷺ was killed.

236
00:15:54,194 --> 00:15:57,647
All of this was Gham(غم) all of this was distress that the Muslims had to go through.

237
00:15:59,107 --> 00:16:01,357
وَلِيُمَحِّصَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا

238
00:16:01,746 --> 00:16:05,087
It's a purification process, it's a selection process.

239
00:16:05,967 --> 00:16:07,136
These are the trials.

240
00:16:08,542 --> 00:16:10,689
And the next and I'm combining these in one,

241
00:16:10,767 --> 00:16:13,882
 even though they could be separated as two different lessons,

242
00:16:14,355 --> 00:16:15,989
وَيَمْحَقَ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

243
00:16:16,045 --> 00:16:17,648
And destroy the disbelievers

244
00:16:18,403 --> 00:16:22,966
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ dislikes some of the Kuffar(كفار), so much

245
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:27,836
that they have places for them reserved in Hellfire

246
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:32,515
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ destroys them through their actions in Duniyah(دنيا).

247
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:36,114
So the fact that the Kuffar(كفار) defeated the Muslims

248
00:16:36,506 --> 00:16:38,471
and killed 70 of them,

249
00:16:39,028 --> 00:16:43,314
and the Muslims had to suffer all of this hardship under the hands of the kuffar(كفار).

250
00:16:43,624 --> 00:16:47,321
This is destruction for the kuffar(كفار), it's not something for them to be happy about.

251
00:16:48,224 --> 00:16:50,523
For Ibn Qamiyah(ابن قميه) to strike Rasool Allah ﷺ,

252
00:16:50,563 --> 00:16:53,030
and Ut'bah Bin Abi Waqas(عتبة بن ابي وقاص) to strike Rasool Allah ﷺ

253
00:16:53,316 --> 00:16:55,391
is that good news for them?

254
00:16:55,647 --> 00:16:57,200
Is that something to be happy about?

255
00:16:58,006 --> 00:17:00,843
That is the worst thing that ever happened to them in their lives.

256
00:17:01,364 --> 00:17:04,103
And they would be condemned to Hellfire for eternity for it.

257
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:06,880
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ dislikes some of the Kuffar(كفار)

258
00:17:06,969 --> 00:17:10,134
and they deserve His damnation and eternal punishment,

259
00:17:10,347 --> 00:17:13,092
because of the actions that they committed in Duniyah(دنيا).

260
00:17:13,834 --> 00:17:16,809
So, when we see that a certain nation of Kuffr(كفر),

261
00:17:17,872 --> 00:17:22,040
it appears that it has free reign to do whatever it wants with the Muslims

262
00:17:22,175 --> 00:17:24,854
to kill some of them in whichever country it wants.

263
00:17:25,231 --> 00:17:28,494
And to round them up, interrogate them, torture them,

264
00:17:28,782 --> 00:17:33,338
throw them in prisons for years at end without any due course of law.

265
00:17:34,327 --> 00:17:36,323
Is that good news for them.

266
00:17:36,584 --> 00:17:40,723
That's a sign that Allahعَزّوجَلّ is angry with this nation or people,

267
00:17:40,929 --> 00:17:44,387
that's a sign that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has His wrath on them,

268
00:17:44,676 --> 00:17:47,746
that's a sign of what will happen to them on the Day of Judgment.

269
00:17:48,168 --> 00:17:52,429
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives these tyrants chance in Duniyah(دنيا)

270
00:17:53,435 --> 00:18:00,354
so that they could achieve rightfully and claim their places in hellfire.

271
00:18:01,278 --> 00:18:07,296
One should not think this is a sign that Muslims are weak or that this religion will defeated.

272
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:13,331
 No, this is an indication and we could for example, bring up the example of Firauon(فرعون)

273
00:18:13,999 --> 00:18:18,097
how he succeeded in punishing the children of Israel(اسرائيل) for years.

274
00:18:18,813 --> 00:18:21,031
Is that something for Firauon(فرعون) to be happy about?

275
00:18:21,142 --> 00:18:25,623
 No, that was because Allahعَزّوجَلّ was building a case against him.

276
00:18:25,892 --> 00:18:30,078
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ was gathering evidence against him to be presented on the Day of Judgment.

277
00:18:30,135 --> 00:18:33,373
And that's exactly what's happening with the enemies of Allah today.

278
00:18:33,413 --> 00:18:35,109
 Allah is building a case against them.

279
00:18:35,649 --> 00:18:37,553
Don't think that they will escape justice.

280
00:18:37,861 --> 00:18:40,228
Allahعَزّوجَلّ sees and hears everything.

281
00:18:40,537 --> 00:18:45,355
And on the Day of Judgment, all of what they have done will be presented to them

282
00:18:45,683 --> 00:18:47,880
in the court of justice of the Day of Judgment.

283
00:18:47,904 --> 00:18:50,352
That's why it's called Al-Yaom Ul Qayamah(اليوم القيامة), the day of Judgment,

284
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:55,289
Yaum Ul Hissaab(يوم الحساب), because Allahعَزّوجَلّ will judge upon them.

285
00:18:55,802 --> 00:18:59,616
 And all of this evidence will be presented to them nothing will be hidden,

286
00:18:59,904 --> 00:19:01,079
لاَ تَخْفَى عَلَيْهِ خَافِيَةٌ

287
00:19:01,119 --> 00:19:04,524
Nothing is hidden from the eyes of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, the All knowing.

288
00:19:05,108 --> 00:19:08,568
So, this is a Hikmah(حكمة) that you shouldn't neglect or overlook.

289
00:19:09,612 --> 00:19:13,496
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is building a case against the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

290
00:19:13,704 --> 00:19:16,474
 Because Allah knows the evil of their heart,

291
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:19,844
Allahعَزّوجَلّ makes it manifest through their actions,

292
00:19:20,656 --> 00:19:22,820
so that they wouldn't come on the day of judgment and say,

293
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:26,282
O Allah, how come you're casting us into Hellfire

294
00:19:26,551 --> 00:19:28,229
when we haven't done any evil,

295
00:19:28,501 --> 00:19:31,893
so even though Allahعَزّوجَلّ already knows what is in their hearts,

296
00:19:31,933 --> 00:19:36,833
Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives them a chance to play it out in the real world,

297
00:19:37,313 --> 00:19:40,158
so that they wouldn't have any excuse on the Day of Judgment.

298
00:19:41,936 --> 00:19:43,055
The sixth lesson,

299
00:19:43,507 --> 00:19:49,882
أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ وَيَعْلَمَ الصَّابِرِينَ۝

300
00:19:50,591 --> 00:19:53,462
For those Muslims, who thought that Islam is a free ride,

301
00:19:53,974 --> 00:19:55,926
that Islam is convenient

302
00:19:56,371 --> 00:20:00,911
that Islam will give you paradise, without demanding too much from you,

303
00:20:00,951 --> 00:20:05,675
all what you have to do is give a few Rak'ah(ركعة) here and there, for Allahعَزّوجَلّ, duing the day

304
00:20:05,946 --> 00:20:07,952
and make a few Azkaar(ازكار) and that's it.

305
00:20:07,992 --> 00:20:09,193
You're granted Paradise,

306
00:20:09,344 --> 00:20:11,304
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling such people.

307
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:14,171
Or do you think that you will enter Paradise,

308
00:20:14,211 --> 00:20:18,106
while Allah has not made evident those of you, who fight Jihad(جهاد) in His cause

309
00:20:18,483 --> 00:20:20,985
and made evident, those who are steadfast.

310
00:20:21,710 --> 00:20:24,643
Don't think that you can make it to Jannah(جنه) without Jihad(جهاد) Feesabil Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله).

311
00:20:25,923 --> 00:20:28,500
وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا مِنْكُمْ

312
00:20:29,048 --> 00:20:33,338
Allah is telling the Muslims, you're going to have to go through these stages

313
00:20:33,708 --> 00:20:34,773
 you have to go through it.

314
00:20:35,372 --> 00:20:39,078
Because you cannot claim your place in Jannah(جنة),

315
00:20:39,427 --> 00:20:43,019
without going through the test of Jihad Feesabeel Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله).

316
00:20:43,249 --> 00:20:50,444
And consequently, it will show your steadfastness because that's where Sabar(صبر) is shown.

317
00:20:51,354 --> 00:20:55,850
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, this is the Islamic way.

318
00:20:56,258 --> 00:20:57,571
This is the Islamic way.

319
00:20:57,872 --> 00:21:03,134
This is not a mystic religion, where you could do a few Azkaar(اذكار) here and there

320
00:21:03,174 --> 00:21:05,436
 and then think that you have done your part,

321
00:21:05,642 --> 00:21:06,189
No,

322
00:21:06,245 --> 00:21:08,333
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is going to test you in the field.

323
00:21:08,813 --> 00:21:11,777
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has some serious demands from you.

324
00:21:12,064 --> 00:21:14,242
Because Allahعَزّوجَلّ is giving you Jannah(جنة).

325
00:21:14,850 --> 00:21:16,424
I mean, you're not gonna get it for free.

326
00:21:16,818 --> 00:21:18,518
You have to earn it, you have to work for it.

327
00:21:18,631 --> 00:21:22,322
When I say, earn it, it's not literal,

328
00:21:22,362 --> 00:21:28,378
because no matter what we do, Jannah(جنة) is more than our deeds.

329
00:21:29,043 --> 00:21:34,267
Even Rasool Allah ﷺ said that I will only get into Jannah(جنة), by the mercy of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

330
00:21:35,871 --> 00:21:37,994
So again, but Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants us to do our best.

331
00:21:38,543 --> 00:21:46,851
He wants us to the utmost effort that we are capable of, humanly in this Duniyah(دنيا).

332
00:21:48,001 --> 00:21:49,045
Seventh lesson,

333
00:21:49,728 --> 00:21:54,208
after the Battle of Badr(بدر), and the outstanding victory of Muslims,

334
00:21:54,819 --> 00:21:59,238
the ones who missed it, they were looking forward to meeting the enemy again.

335
00:21:59,261 --> 00:22:04,079
 And they were asking for Shahadah(شهاده) and they were asking for meeting death.

336
00:22:04,879 --> 00:22:07,850
But that was all, desires in the heart.

337
00:22:08,425 --> 00:22:12,274
How it's going to play out in the real world is something else.

338
00:22:12,644 --> 00:22:14,340
So, you could have the intention.

339
00:22:14,739 --> 00:22:16,624
 But is that intention real?

340
00:22:17,049 --> 00:22:18,227
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

341
00:22:18,457 --> 00:22:31,246
وَلَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ تَلْقَوْهُ فَقَدْ رَأَيْتُمُوهُ وَأَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُونَ۝

342
00:22:31,711 --> 00:22:34,922
And you had certainly wished for death, i.e. martyrdom

343
00:22:35,174 --> 00:22:36,680
before you encountered it.

344
00:22:37,021 --> 00:22:41,829
And you have now seen it before you, while you were looking on.

345
00:22:42,488 --> 00:22:48,573
So, in other words, actual fighting was necessary to verify whether their wishes were true or not,

346
00:22:48,728 --> 00:22:50,602
whether their intentions were true or not.

347
00:22:50,918 --> 00:22:53,576
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) maybe even they didn't know about it.

348
00:22:53,656 --> 00:22:58,251
I mean, you could, every one of us could have intentions in their hearts.

349
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:00,148
But does that mean that

350
00:23:00,228 --> 00:23:05,865
if we are faced with an opportunity to fulfill those intentions, we would really fulfill them.

351
00:23:06,215 --> 00:23:08,176
That is something that only Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows

352
00:23:08,216 --> 00:23:14,501
and that's why Allahعَزّوجَلّ made them face these situations to make evident what was in their hearts.

353
00:23:15,438 --> 00:23:17,708
So, Allah is telling them, You want to face martyrdom.?

354
00:23:17,943 --> 00:23:18,832
Here you go.

355
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:22,737
Here's your chance.! Go ahead.! Show me.

356
00:23:23,201 --> 00:23:30,477
So, these are seven lessons we can learn from verses 140, 143 of Surat Al-Imran(سورة العمران).

357
00:23:31,469 --> 00:23:33,461
Next, treating mistakes

358
00:23:34,506 --> 00:23:38,941
How did Allahعَزّوجَلّ deal with the mistakes of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم?

359
00:23:39,992 --> 00:23:41,394
First let me say this.

360
00:23:41,981 --> 00:23:49,704
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has never ever praised the Muslims for their victories, never.

361
00:23:50,518 --> 00:23:51,843
So, after the Battle of Badr(بدر)

362
00:23:51,883 --> 00:23:57,264
Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an are not coming down, thanking the Muslims and praising them for their efforts in Badr(بدر),

363
00:23:57,643 --> 00:24:00,675
No! It was infact, to the contrary.

364
00:24:00,715 --> 00:24:02,061
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

365
00:24:02,465 --> 00:24:09,600
وَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشْرَىٰ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ بِهِ قُلُوبُكُمْ  ۗ

366
00:24:09,938 --> 00:24:18,018
وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ اِنَّ اللهَ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ۝

367
00:24:18,990 --> 00:24:20,161
Victory is from Allah,

368
00:24:21,381 --> 00:24:23,750
so I'm not giving you credit for that victory in Badr(بدر)

369
00:24:24,714 --> 00:24:31,800
and in the Battle of Badr(بدر), if you recall we talked about the dispute over the prisoners of war.

370
00:24:32,189 --> 00:24:34,292
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed then,

371
00:24:35,165 --> 00:24:40,237
 actually it was about the prisoners of war Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed.

372
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:50,487
لَوْلَا كِتَابٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ۝

373
00:24:51,411 --> 00:24:54,081
If not for a decree from Allah that preceded,

374
00:24:54,437 --> 00:24:57,758
you would have been touched for, what you took by great punishment.

375
00:24:58,021 --> 00:25:01,244
So, after the Battle of Badr(بدر), Allah told them, that I was going to punish you.

376
00:25:01,868 --> 00:25:06,670
So, to the contrary, one would think that Allah would assume that since they have won,

377
00:25:06,998 --> 00:25:08,701
the Ayaat(آيات) would come praising them, no.

378
00:25:08,736 --> 00:25:11,005
Allahعَزّوجَلّ was threatening them with punishment,

379
00:25:11,291 --> 00:25:13,978
because of what they have done with the prisoners of war.

380
00:25:14,695 --> 00:25:17,291
And Allah said that because you are interested in Duniyah(دنيا),

381
00:25:17,316 --> 00:25:18,883
because you wanted the ransom.

382
00:25:19,323 --> 00:25:23,603
You did not execute the prisoners, when that is the course of action that you have taken.

383
00:25:23,907 --> 00:25:26,347
 So, it was because of your love of Duniyah(دنيا),

384
00:25:26,681 --> 00:25:32,287
you have chosen to ransom the prisoners of war and Allah said that I was going to punish you.

385
00:25:33,262 --> 00:25:34,940
If it wasn't in the my book,

386
00:25:35,193 --> 00:25:38,372
that ransom is Halal(حلال) for you, you would have been punished.

387
00:25:39,362 --> 00:25:40,761
While in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

388
00:25:41,029 --> 00:25:44,921
let's compare the Ayaat(آيات) of Badr(بدر) with the Ayaat(آيات) of Uhud(أحَد),

389
00:25:44,945 --> 00:25:46,750
here in Badr(بدر), I was going to punish you,

390
00:25:46,794 --> 00:25:48,015
what about in Uhud(أحَد)?

391
00:25:48,147 --> 00:25:49,219
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

392
00:25:49,370 --> 00:25:52,743
وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْ ۗ وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

393
00:25:53,789 --> 00:25:58,710
And He has already forgiven you and Allah is the possessor of bounty for the believers.

394
00:25:58,995 --> 00:26:00,636
So, after the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

395
00:26:01,136 --> 00:26:04,261
when they were at fault, and they lost, Allah said;

396
00:26:04,781 --> 00:26:05,884
And I have forgiven you,

397
00:26:06,090 --> 00:26:09,027
while after the Battle of Badr(بدر), Allah said, I was going to punish you.

398
00:26:09,506 --> 00:26:10,773
This tells us something.

399
00:26:11,035 --> 00:26:17,116
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is curing our hearts from any diseases that might linger in it.

400
00:26:17,331 --> 00:26:18,659
After the Battle of Badr(بدر),

401
00:26:19,241 --> 00:26:26,088
to save the Muslims from feelings of pride or arrogance.

402
00:26:26,691 --> 00:26:30,278
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has said that I was going to punish you for what you have done.

403
00:26:31,743 --> 00:26:35,566
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ said that victory that you have achieved is actually from Me,

404
00:26:36,351 --> 00:26:37,799
while after the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

405
00:26:38,028 --> 00:26:40,253
because they have already suffered in Duniyah(دنيا).

406
00:26:40,689 --> 00:26:43,732
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is raising up their spirits again,

407
00:26:43,891 --> 00:26:47,623
and comforting them by telling them that I have forgiven you.

408
00:26:48,380 --> 00:26:51,870
You have committed a mistake on that hill, by coming down

409
00:26:52,775 --> 00:26:55,761
and you have committed a sin by disobeying the Prophet.

410
00:26:56,869 --> 00:27:01,789
And you have committed a sin by being thirsty and hungry for Duniyah(دنيا).

411
00:27:02,239 --> 00:27:04,906
But in the end, I have forgiven you.

412
00:27:07,319 --> 00:27:08,319
Next lesson,

413
00:27:08,565 --> 00:27:14,476
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is turning our attention to the previous Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

414
00:27:15,540 --> 00:27:19,200
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in verses 146 to 148.

415
00:27:19,458 --> 00:27:28,248
وَكَأَيِّنْ مِنْ نَبِيٍّ قَاتَلَ مَعَهُ رِبِّيُّونَ كَثِيرٌ فَمَا وَهَنُوا

416
00:27:28,471 --> 00:27:37,150
فَمَا وَهَنُوا لِمَا أَصَابَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَمَا ضَعُفُوا وَمَا اسْتَكَانُوا ۗ

417
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:42,600
وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الصَّابِرِينَ۝

418
00:27:42,947 --> 00:27:54,673
 وَمَا كَانَ قَوْلَهُمْ إِلَّا أَنْ قَالُوا رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَإِسْرَافَنَا فِي أَمْرِنَا

419
00:27:55,076 --> 00:28:07,608
رَبَّنَا اغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَإِسْرَافَنَا فِي أَمْرِنَا وَثَبِّتْ أَقْدَامَنَا وَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

420
00:28:08,102 --> 00:28:14,430
 فَآتَاهُمُ اللَّهُ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا وَحُسْنَ ثَوَابِ الْآخِرَةِ ۗ

421
00:28:14,652 --> 00:28:19,131
وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ۝

422
00:28:19,365 --> 00:28:25,341
And how many a prophet fought and with him fought many religious scholars,

423
00:28:26,017 --> 00:28:30,337
but they never lost assurance, due to what afflicted them in the cause of Allah.

424
00:28:30,786 --> 00:28:32,985
Nor did they weaken or submit

425
00:28:33,241 --> 00:28:35,125
and Allah loves the steadfast.

426
00:28:35,930 --> 00:28:38,483
And their words were not but that they said

427
00:28:38,563 --> 00:28:43,542
 O our Lord, forgive us our sins and the excess committed in our affairs

428
00:28:43,934 --> 00:28:48,207
and plant firmly our feet and give us victory over the disbelieving people.

429
00:28:48,574 --> 00:28:51,491
So, Allah gave them the reward of this world.

430
00:28:51,740 --> 00:28:56,293
And the good reward of the hereafter and Allah loves the doers of good.

431
00:28:58,970 --> 00:29:00,620
What can we learn from these Ayaat(آيات),

432
00:29:01,044 --> 00:29:05,169
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that the prophets before you fought

433
00:29:05,619 --> 00:29:08,440
and alongside them fought religious scholars,

434
00:29:08,814 --> 00:29:11,526
so the scholars should not sit at home,

435
00:29:11,917 --> 00:29:14,828
they should stand with their Prophets and fight.

436
00:29:16,658 --> 00:29:22,365
You know, because scholars tend to develop a tradition, and this is with scholars among every religion,

437
00:29:22,723 --> 00:29:26,136
after a while because of all of the respect that they get from the people,

438
00:29:26,565 --> 00:29:28,390
they kind of develop this special status.

439
00:29:28,462 --> 00:29:32,049
So, they wear special clothes, and they act in a special way.

440
00:29:32,257 --> 00:29:35,668
And it could be superficies, it could be ceremonial,

441
00:29:36,153 --> 00:29:42,160
and they would stay away from the dirt and the that the soldiers have to suffer,

442
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:48,725
you know, walking in the dirt and sleeping in bunker beds or maybe not even sleeping beds at all

443
00:29:49,114 --> 00:29:53,440
and suffering the pain and you know, being equal to everybody else,

444
00:29:53,517 --> 00:29:55,906
and going through that hard life.

445
00:29:56,275 --> 00:29:58,424
 Probably Shaytaan(شيطان) can come to this scholar and say

446
00:29:58,498 --> 00:30:01,958
 you know, you don't have to go through all of that you have Ilm(علم), you have knowledge,

447
00:30:01,997 --> 00:30:04,238
 just stay at home and teach the people that would be enough.

448
00:30:04,434 --> 00:30:08,299
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying here that, that's not the way of the righteous scholars,

449
00:30:08,349 --> 00:30:11,164
the righteous scholars stood with their Prophets, they were in the field.

450
00:30:12,432 --> 00:30:17,082
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ said, but they never lost assurance due to what afflicted them.

451
00:30:17,301 --> 00:30:20,230
So, when they lost when they were faced with hardship,

452
00:30:20,737 --> 00:30:22,106
they never lost assurance.

453
00:30:23,052 --> 00:30:27,633
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, don't be affected by the setback.

454
00:30:28,846 --> 00:30:30,213
Don't let it pull you down.

455
00:30:31,514 --> 00:30:34,048
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ said, it didn't weaken them.

456
00:30:34,314 --> 00:30:39,247
And they didn't submit, and Allah loves the steadfast, you have to carry on, persist.

457
00:30:40,954 --> 00:30:46,974
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that they said, Our Lord, forgive us our sins,

458
00:30:47,405 --> 00:30:49,898
and the excess committed in our affairs.

459
00:30:50,565 --> 00:30:54,315
This is very important that when you're fighting for the sake of Allah,

460
00:30:54,667 --> 00:30:57,810
you don't depend on your numbers or your preparation,

461
00:30:58,055 --> 00:30:59,324
but you depend on Allah

462
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:01,114
and you seek forgiveness from Him.

463
00:31:01,264 --> 00:31:02,978
أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ

464
00:31:03,094 --> 00:31:05,362
And you admit your sins,

465
00:31:05,661 --> 00:31:12,886
 and you humble yourself in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, you humiliate yourself under Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

466
00:31:13,106 --> 00:31:16,785
 That is something that Allahعَزّوجَلّ loves to see from His servants

467
00:31:17,050 --> 00:31:20,539
and that is what these Mujahideen(مجاهدين) before Muhammadﷺ did.

468
00:31:20,619 --> 00:31:26,110
See Allahعَزّوجَلّ is bringing the story of these early fighters for the Muslims to learn.

469
00:31:26,703 --> 00:31:28,555
So, Allah is saying this was their way.

470
00:31:29,299 --> 00:31:35,478
And then they would say and plant firmly our feet and give us victory, after they admit their sins.

471
00:31:35,979 --> 00:31:37,552
And they ask Allah for forgiveness.

472
00:31:38,119 --> 00:31:43,617
And that is when Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given them reward of this life and the reward of the afterlife.

473
00:31:43,963 --> 00:31:45,844
And Allah loves the doers of good.

474
00:31:46,996 --> 00:31:52,604
And since Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling the Muslims to turn their attention to the fighters of the former nations,

475
00:31:52,862 --> 00:31:57,318
now we have the former nations and also the fighters of this Ummah(امة),

476
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:00,341
we have twice the lessons that the Sahabah(صحابه) had.

477
00:32:01,114 --> 00:32:03,249
Because now we have their example with us.

478
00:32:04,426 --> 00:32:09,689
The next lesson, the evil of disobedience, the consequences of disobedience.

479
00:32:10,960 --> 00:32:14,456
Disobeying Rasool Allah ﷺ is very dangerous.

480
00:32:15,575 --> 00:32:17,573
That is why they lost in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

481
00:32:17,786 --> 00:32:20,070
because of disobeying Rasool Allah ﷺ.

482
00:32:20,858 --> 00:32:21,927
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

483
00:32:22,215 --> 00:32:33,113
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنْكُمْ ۖ

484
00:32:33,676 --> 00:32:47,017
فَإِنْ تَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي شَيْءٍ فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ ۚ

485
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:52,830
ذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ وَأَحْسَنُ تَأْوِيلًا۝

486
00:32:53,276 --> 00:32:58,415
O, you have believed obey Allah and obey the messenger and those in authority among you.

487
00:32:58,975 --> 00:33:02,296
So, after the Messenger of Allah, we obey the Ameer(امير).

488
00:33:02,701 --> 00:33:07,050
And if you disagree over anything referred to Allah and the messenger,

489
00:33:08,008 --> 00:33:12,929
if you should believe in Allah and the last day, that is the best way and the best result,

490
00:33:13,496 --> 00:33:18,390
if we have a dispute on any affair, we take it back to Qur'an and Sunnah(سنة),

491
00:33:19,639 --> 00:33:20,858
that is our reference.

492
00:33:21,427 --> 00:33:25,234
The next lesson, the danger of preferring Duniya(دنيا) over Aaakhirah(آخرة).

493
00:33:26,130 --> 00:33:30,309
You know, the story of this Ummah(امة) with the booty war is a sad one.

494
00:33:31,298 --> 00:33:32,803
It started in the Battle of Badr(بدر),

495
00:33:32,934 --> 00:33:35,949
that's when Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Aayaat(آيات) of Al-Anfaal(الانفال).

496
00:33:36,012 --> 00:33:38,258
Ubadah Bin Samit(عبادة بن سامت) said these Ayaat(آيات) were revealed,

497
00:33:38,515 --> 00:33:42,814
because we the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ disputed over the booty,

498
00:33:43,057 --> 00:33:45,299
and our manners were not appropriate

499
00:33:45,488 --> 00:33:46,835
وَسَاءتْ فِيْه اَخْلَاقُنَا

500
00:33:48,236 --> 00:33:49,519
And in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

501
00:33:50,024 --> 00:33:52,749
That was what brought down the archers.

502
00:33:53,595 --> 00:33:58,986
It was because they were eager to participate in collecting the booty.

503
00:33:59,813 --> 00:34:03,279
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) this problem carried on.

504
00:34:03,852 --> 00:34:05,962
And yes, they were Muslims, who learn the lessons.

505
00:34:06,017 --> 00:34:07,407
But there were others who didn't.

506
00:34:08,105 --> 00:34:16,245
What stopped, the Muslim conquest, in Western Europe was booty.

507
00:34:16,881 --> 00:34:20,546
The Muslims, when they entered into Spain,

508
00:34:21,229 --> 00:34:25,083
Abdur Rahmaan Al-Ghafiqi(عبد الرحمن الغافقي), was the Ameer(امير) of the Muslims.

509
00:34:25,123 --> 00:34:27,322
 And he was leading them into France now.

510
00:34:27,660 --> 00:34:33,599
And they succeeded in conquering almost two thirds of France.

511
00:34:34,142 --> 00:34:38,183
And they were 100 kilometers away from Paris, the capital

512
00:34:38,642 --> 00:34:42,011
and they were almost going to run over France.

513
00:34:42,666 --> 00:34:48,612
But by the time they reached to the outskirts of Paris,

514
00:34:49,367 --> 00:34:51,341
they were loaded with booties,

515
00:34:51,579 --> 00:34:53,960
loaded with spoils of war.

516
00:34:54,673 --> 00:34:58,033
So, now the soldier is fighting the enemy in front of him,

517
00:34:58,087 --> 00:34:59,641
but his mind is behind him.

518
00:34:59,681 --> 00:35:05,707
He's thinking about his share of the booties of war, all of this stuff that we're carrying with us,

519
00:35:06,295 --> 00:35:08,619
and it was pulling down the army.

520
00:35:09,350 --> 00:35:13,832
So, they ended up losing in the battle called Balaat Ush-Shuhadaah(بلاط الشهدآء),

521
00:35:14,084 --> 00:35:15,262
the court of martyrs

522
00:35:15,302 --> 00:35:20,643
and it was given this name because of the huge number of Muslims, who were killed in that battle.

523
00:35:20,899 --> 00:35:26,512
Among them, one of the greatest leaders of the Muslim armies, Abdur Rahmaan Al-Ghafiqi رحمه الله,

524
00:35:26,664 --> 00:35:27,900
he was killed in that battle,

525
00:35:28,150 --> 00:35:32,298
and that marked the end of the Muslim advanced in Western Europe.

526
00:35:32,753 --> 00:35:37,314
They never reach there again. From there on, it was retreat, retreat, retreat.

527
00:35:38,807 --> 00:35:41,607
Even though it was a bit slow, it took about 800 years,

528
00:35:41,977 --> 00:35:44,925
but it was slowly but surely.

529
00:35:46,225 --> 00:35:51,028
So, the turning point was due to booty.

530
00:35:52,793 --> 00:35:54,626
Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه said,

531
00:35:54,658 --> 00:35:59,188
I did not know that there was among us, the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

532
00:35:59,603 --> 00:36:03,480
 people who preferred Duniyah(دنيا) over Aakhirah(آخرة).

533
00:36:03,830 --> 00:36:05,751
You know this is not talking about Al-Munafiqeen(المنافقين),

534
00:36:05,858 --> 00:36:07,744
this is talking about some of the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين).

535
00:36:09,251 --> 00:36:13,476
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, among you are some, who desire this world

536
00:36:13,728 --> 00:36:16,943
and among you are some who desire the hereafter.

537
00:36:17,289 --> 00:36:22,637
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that in the hearts of some of you there's the desire of Duniyah(دنيا).

538
00:36:23,227 --> 00:36:24,298
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said;

539
00:36:24,338 --> 00:36:29,299
I never knew that existed among some of the Sahabah(صحابه), until then.

540
00:36:29,722 --> 00:36:31,151
And this again shows you,

541
00:36:31,191 --> 00:36:38,652
how Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) brought out something that possibly could have never showed up to the surface.

542
00:36:39,231 --> 00:36:41,723
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: I didn't know that it existed.

543
00:36:42,691 --> 00:36:46,620
Next lesson, we should hold on fast to our religion.

544
00:36:47,545 --> 00:36:51,385
When the rumors spread that Muhammadﷺ was killed

545
00:36:51,869 --> 00:36:57,733
some of the Muslims were trying to find a way to meet with Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابيئ)

546
00:36:57,813 --> 00:37:04,252
to have him intercede with the Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), to give them truce.

547
00:37:05,275 --> 00:37:08,217
Allahعَزّوجَلّ taught us a lesson, Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

548
00:37:08,561 --> 00:37:15,984
وَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ ۚ

549
00:37:16,254 --> 00:37:22,677
أَفَإِنْ مَاتَ أَوْ قُتِلَ انْقَلَبْتُمْ عَلَىٰ أعْقَابِكُمْ ۚ

550
00:37:22,819 --> 00:37:29,728
وَمَنْ يَنْقَلِبْ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ فَلَنْ يَضُرَّ اللَّهَ شَيْئًا ۗ

551
00:37:29,982 --> 00:37:33,584
وَسَيَجْزِي اللَّهُ الشَّاكِرِينَ۝

552
00:37:33,868 --> 00:37:36,567
Muhammad(محمد) is not but a messenger.

553
00:37:37,156 --> 00:37:39,775
Other messengers have passed on before him.

554
00:37:40,411 --> 00:37:45,549
Muhammadﷺ is a messenger and there are other messengers before him and where are they now?

555
00:37:45,721 --> 00:37:46,507
They're dead.

556
00:37:47,507 --> 00:37:56,303
So, the same thing, death, should be expected to happen to Muhammadﷺ, if all of the other prophets are dead.

557
00:37:56,696 --> 00:38:00,040
Why do you think or assume that Muhammadﷺ wouldn't die as they did?

558
00:38:00,902 --> 00:38:04,657
And then Allah said, so if he was to die or to be killed?

559
00:38:04,910 --> 00:38:07,934
Would you then turn back on your heels to unbelief?

560
00:38:08,568 --> 00:38:10,527
Is that how you're going to react his death

561
00:38:10,731 --> 00:38:13,622
 just because Muhammadﷺ died you're going to give up your religion.

562
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:18,518
And he who turns back on his heels will never harm Allah at all,

563
00:38:19,205 --> 00:38:21,413
you are the ones who need Allah, Allah doesn't need you.

564
00:38:21,795 --> 00:38:23,730
But Allah will reward the Grateful.

565
00:38:24,992 --> 00:38:26,533
This is Al-Imran(العمران) One (hundred) fouty four(144).

566
00:38:26,901 --> 00:38:32,129
Therefore Allah telling us that this religion does not depend on personalities.

567
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:36,003
The fate of this religion is not hinged to any person

568
00:38:36,130 --> 00:38:41,372
even if that person is the great and noble person of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

569
00:38:42,035 --> 00:38:44,306
So, if that's the case with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

570
00:38:44,610 --> 00:38:49,433
we should never think or believe if such and such person is killed,

571
00:38:49,565 --> 00:38:52,752
that this religion the advance of this religion will stop,

572
00:38:52,895 --> 00:38:59,625
we should never assume that the victory is dependent on a particular leader.

573
00:39:00,214 --> 00:39:07,873
And that's why Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) fired Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه from his post of the general of the Muslim armies.

574
00:39:08,401 --> 00:39:11,879
He wanted people to know that victory is not because of Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد),

575
00:39:12,188 --> 00:39:13,780
victory is because of Allah.

576
00:39:14,706 --> 00:39:17,689
It is Allah, Who brought us victory, it is not Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد).

577
00:39:18,384 --> 00:39:23,228
So, Muslims who are waiting now for a particular leader or are depending on a particular leader,

578
00:39:23,448 --> 00:39:25,031
you should depend on Allah.

579
00:39:25,928 --> 00:39:28,956
Allah did not allow the Muslims to depend on Muhammadﷺ,

580
00:39:29,249 --> 00:39:33,617
Allah told them if Muhammad(محمد) dies, you need to carry on, being Muslims,

581
00:39:33,697 --> 00:39:36,490
carry on spreading the message as if nothing changed.

582
00:39:36,928 --> 00:39:39,920
You should not retreat and fall back on your heels.

583
00:39:41,464 --> 00:39:43,628
Because this religion is dependent on, No One

584
00:39:44,006 --> 00:39:49,357
and that's why when Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه came to Madina after the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

585
00:39:49,397 --> 00:39:50,878
What did he say to the people.

586
00:39:51,658 --> 00:39:54,325
مَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُوْ مُحَمَّدً فَاِنَّ مُحَمَّدً قَدْ مَاتْ

587
00:39:54,675 --> 00:39:57,373
، وَمَنْ كَانَ يَعْبُدُالله فَاِنَّ الله حَيُّ الَّا يَمُوْتْ

588
00:39:57,719 --> 00:40:00,233
Whoever worships Muhammad(محمد), Muhammad(محمد) is dead.

589
00:40:00,775 --> 00:40:04,013
But whoever worships Allah, Allah is alive and never dies.

590
00:40:05,199 --> 00:40:09,018
How did the Prophet deal with the archers and the hypocrites,

591
00:40:09,641 --> 00:40:13,376
the archers disobeyed him and the hypocrites also disobeyed him.

592
00:40:13,944 --> 00:40:15,350
So, how did he deal with them?

593
00:40:15,594 --> 00:40:16,703
He dealt with him differently.

594
00:40:16,973 --> 00:40:19,002
Let's look at how he dealt with the archers.

595
00:40:19,535 --> 00:40:20,869
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

596
00:40:21,549 --> 00:40:26,316
فَبِمَا رَحْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ لِنْتَ لَهُمْ ۖ

597
00:40:26,607 --> 00:40:32,693
وَلَوْ كُنْتَ فَظًّا غَلِيظَ الْقَلْبِ لَانْفَضُّوا مِنْ حَوْلِكَ ۖ

598
00:40:33,063 --> 00:40:38,108
فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ وَشَاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ ۖ

599
00:40:38,332 --> 00:40:42,768
فَإِذَا عَزَمْتَ فَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۚ

600
00:40:43,022 --> 00:40:48,204
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ۝

601
00:40:48,556 --> 00:40:51,283
So, by mercy from Allah, O Muhammad(محمد),

602
00:40:51,701 --> 00:40:53,570
you were lenient with them.

603
00:40:54,107 --> 00:40:58,250
And if you had been rude in speech and harsh in heart,

604
00:40:58,834 --> 00:41:01,552
they would have disbanded from about you.

605
00:41:02,559 --> 00:41:04,327
So, Allah is saying Muhammadﷺ,

606
00:41:05,136 --> 00:41:09,573
your method of Da'wah(دعوة) has been based on being lenient, being soft,

607
00:41:10,074 --> 00:41:12,808
not being harsh in word or speech,

608
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:16,531
not being rude in speech or harsh in heart.

609
00:41:17,443 --> 00:41:21,912
That is how, you were able to bring these hearts together.

610
00:41:22,599 --> 00:41:24,215
So, how do you deal with the archers.?

611
00:41:24,255 --> 00:41:28,778
Allah said: So pardon them and ask forgiveness for them.

612
00:41:28,985 --> 00:41:30,107
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله),

613
00:41:30,538 --> 00:41:32,213
we lost because of them,

614
00:41:32,795 --> 00:41:35,442
Rasool Allah ﷺ was injured because of them,

615
00:41:36,009 --> 00:41:39,031
70 Muslims were killed because of them

616
00:41:39,734 --> 00:41:42,356
and then you pardon them and not only pardon them,

617
00:41:42,884 --> 00:41:45,451
but Allah wants you to ask forgiveness for them.

618
00:41:45,669 --> 00:41:47,130
وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ

619
00:41:47,329 --> 00:41:49,221
You Muhammadﷺ, who suffered

620
00:41:49,690 --> 00:41:54,021
because of their mistake, you ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to forgive them.

621
00:41:55,104 --> 00:41:58,549
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), we talked about the Shura(شورى),

622
00:41:59,018 --> 00:42:04,208
and we said that some of the Muslims, the youth, especially and the ones, who missed the Battle of Badr(بدر),

623
00:42:04,468 --> 00:42:07,683
were asking Rasool Allah ﷺ to go out and fight outside Madina.

624
00:42:07,871 --> 00:42:10,186
And we said that this wasn't the opinion of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

625
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:13,932
the opinion of Rasool Ullah that we stay in Madina and fight from within.

626
00:42:14,099 --> 00:42:18,003
And that was the better opinion, it was opinion of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

627
00:42:18,331 --> 00:42:22,987
So, that is also probably one of the reasons why they lost.

628
00:42:23,435 --> 00:42:28,447
Nevertheless, Allahعَزّوجَلّ said and consult them in the matter,

629
00:42:29,196 --> 00:42:33,397
even if consultation has led to your defeat.

630
00:42:34,449 --> 00:42:38,199
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying don't let that prevent you from making Shura(شورى) again.

631
00:42:39,124 --> 00:42:45,932
So, we carry on with Shura(شورى) even if the result of the Shura(شورى) was wrong.

632
00:42:47,191 --> 00:42:49,097
You still carry on with Shura(شورى),

633
00:42:49,605 --> 00:42:52,779
Shura(شورى) is the right way to go.

634
00:42:53,412 --> 00:42:56,588
Look at the lessons, this Ghazwah(غزوة) is loaded with lessons.

635
00:42:57,995 --> 00:43:00,008
Shura(شورى), carry on with Shura(شورى).

636
00:43:00,810 --> 00:43:03,803
And when you have decided, then rely upon Allah.

637
00:43:04,149 --> 00:43:07,405
So, after you make Shura(شورى) and you decide, you go ahead,

638
00:43:07,485 --> 00:43:10,312
 you don't waver, you don't change, you don't oscillate.

639
00:43:11,716 --> 00:43:14,059
Allah loves those, who rely upon Him.

640
00:43:14,099 --> 00:43:15,369
Have Tawwakkul(توكل) in Allah.

641
00:43:16,267 --> 00:43:18,028
So, how do you deal with the archers?

642
00:43:18,218 --> 00:43:19,383
Number one, pardon them.

643
00:43:19,407 --> 00:43:21,282
Number two, ask forgiveness for them.

644
00:43:21,424 --> 00:43:23,273
 Number three, consult them,

645
00:43:24,023 --> 00:43:30,434
consult the Muslims, even if they have given you a wrong opinion, carry on consulting them.

646
00:43:31,220 --> 00:43:36,507
So, if this was the instruction of Allah to the prophet of Allah, who is receiving Wahii(وحي) from Allah.

647
00:43:36,758 --> 00:43:37,999
Who's infallible.

648
00:43:38,514 --> 00:43:42,462
What about the poor, humble men like us?

649
00:43:43,152 --> 00:43:46,009
How important does that make Shura(شورى) for us.

650
00:43:46,909 --> 00:43:48,995
That's how he dealt with the archers.

651
00:43:49,035 --> 00:43:51,106
How did he deal with the Munafiqoon(منافقون)?

652
00:43:51,448 --> 00:43:55,393
Allah says , Surat Al-Imran(العمران) Verse 166, 167.

653
00:43:55,739 --> 00:44:05,497
وَمَا أَصَابَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

654
00:44:05,902 --> 00:44:09,315
وَلِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِينَ نَافَقُوا ۚ

655
00:44:09,505 --> 00:44:15,710
وَقِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا قَاتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَوِ ادْفَعُوا ۖ

656
00:44:16,178 --> 00:44:20,678
قَالُوا لَوْ نَعْلَمُ قِتَالًا لَاتَّبَعْنَاكُمْ ۗ

657
00:44:20,821 --> 00:44:26,151
هُمْ لِلْكُفْرِ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَقْرَبُ مِنْهُمْ لِلْإِيمَانِ ۚ

658
00:44:26,453 --> 00:44:31,819
يَقُولُونَ بِأَفْوَاهِهِمْ مَا لَيْسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ ۗ

659
00:44:31,976 --> 00:44:37,150
وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَكْتُمُونَ۝

660
00:44:38,082 --> 00:44:43,507
And what struck you on the day, the two armies met at Uhud(أحَد), was by the permission of Allah,

661
00:44:43,940 --> 00:44:46,688
 that He might make evident the true believers,

662
00:44:47,190 --> 00:44:50,960
and that He might make evident those who are hypocrites,

663
00:44:51,592 --> 00:44:57,202
for it was said to them come fight in the way of Allah, or at least defend.

664
00:44:57,504 --> 00:45:01,994
 They said, if we had known there would be fighting we would have followed you.

665
00:45:02,380 --> 00:45:06,208
They were nearer to disbelieve that day then to faith,

666
00:45:06,538 --> 00:45:09,729
saying with their mouths, what was not in their hearts

667
00:45:10,118 --> 00:45:12,972
and Allah is the most knowing of what they conceal, that was it.

668
00:45:14,030 --> 00:45:15,909
It was exposing them,

669
00:45:17,231 --> 00:45:18,494
but they were not punished.

670
00:45:19,409 --> 00:45:21,017
That was it, they were just exposed.

671
00:45:21,812 --> 00:45:24,469
So, I want to bring up an important lesson here

672
00:45:25,213 --> 00:45:27,191
There are some Muslims.

673
00:45:27,231 --> 00:45:34,195
In fact, there are entire movements that are based upon this false hypothesis.

674
00:45:34,878 --> 00:45:41,307
There are some Muslims who say that for the Ummah(امة), to succeed and be victorious.

675
00:45:41,998 --> 00:45:44,839
We have to invite them all to truth,

676
00:45:45,260 --> 00:45:48,779
and they all have to obey Allah and avoid sins.

677
00:45:49,188 --> 00:45:54,145
And as long as there are Muslims who don't pray, Muslims who are committing sins, we're not going to win.

678
00:45:54,607 --> 00:46:00,723
And we're not going to win until the Muslims who pray Fajr(فجر) are equal in number to the Muslims who pray Jum'ah(جمعه),

679
00:46:00,948 --> 00:46:03,422
and then they bring you this saying of that Rabbi,

680
00:46:03,462 --> 00:46:10,114
who went and visited the holy Mosque of Jerusalem and said that Jerusalem will fall in Muslim hands,

681
00:46:10,138 --> 00:46:13,700
when the people, who are praying Fajr(فجر) are equal to the people, who are praying Jum'ah(جمعه),

682
00:46:13,861 --> 00:46:16,119
and we start listening to all of this stuff.

683
00:46:16,159 --> 00:46:19,382
 And the Rabbi said, this and Rabbi said this and this Rabbi said that,

684
00:46:19,977 --> 00:46:23,219
as if it's the Rabbi's, who are receiving the Wahee(وحي) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

685
00:46:24,491 --> 00:46:26,947
That's not a correct hypothesis.

686
00:46:27,435 --> 00:46:31,842
There will always be more Muslims who pray Jum'ah(جمعه) than Muslims who pray Fajr(فجر),

687
00:46:32,266 --> 00:46:35,038
And there will always be Muslims who commit sins,

688
00:46:35,433 --> 00:46:39,310
there will always be Muslims, who commit major sins,

689
00:46:39,739 --> 00:46:44,452
there will always be Muslims who are not fulfilling the obligations,

690
00:46:44,647 --> 00:46:46,323
this will always be the case.

691
00:46:46,708 --> 00:46:49,106
And if you are waiting for victory to come,

692
00:46:49,486 --> 00:46:53,655
when all Muslims are righteous, and all Muslims are Auleaa(إولياء) of Allah, that will never happen.

693
00:46:54,629 --> 00:46:57,401
And to prove to you that this hypothesis is wrong,

694
00:46:57,732 --> 00:47:01,955
is the fact that one third of the Muslim army defected.

695
00:47:02,603 --> 00:47:03,932
Those were the Munafiqoon(منافقون)

696
00:47:04,162 --> 00:47:08,146
 and this did not affect the outcome of the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

697
00:47:08,898 --> 00:47:14,269
The Munafiqoon(منافقون), who left with Abdullah Bin Obaey(عبدالله بن أبي), were not the reason for the Muslim defeat.

698
00:47:15,111 --> 00:47:19,228
This wasn't mentioned as a reason in Sunnah(سنة) and it's not mentioned as a reason in Qur'an,

699
00:47:19,535 --> 00:47:21,956
therefore it's not one of the reasons,

700
00:47:22,484 --> 00:47:25,848
it's not the reason, it's not even one of the reasons, why the Muslims lost.

701
00:47:26,398 --> 00:47:31,217
The joining of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) or their defection wouldn't have made a difference.

702
00:47:32,539 --> 00:47:37,185
And since there will always be Munafiqoon(منافقون) living among the Muslim Ummah(امة),

703
00:47:38,070 --> 00:47:42,857
they will not affect the outcome of the battle between good and evil.

704
00:47:43,573 --> 00:47:49,161
The outcome is affected by the core group of Muslims.

705
00:47:49,922 --> 00:47:51,453
The Taifah Al-Mansourah(الطائفة المنصوره),

706
00:47:51,701 --> 00:47:56,226
Rasool Allah ﷺ has talk about a core group of Muslims called Taifah Al-Mansourah(الطائفة المنصوره).

707
00:47:56,517 --> 00:47:58,241
This is the saved group,

708
00:47:58,468 --> 00:48:01,952
it is these, who have to be on the straight path.

709
00:48:02,737 --> 00:48:05,849
If they start sinning, then the Muslims will lose.

710
00:48:06,512 --> 00:48:08,569
So, the outcome depends on them.

711
00:48:08,619 --> 00:48:10,939
It doesn't depend on all of the Ummah(امة),

712
00:48:11,194 --> 00:48:17,133
see, the Ummah(امة) contains within its ranks, the righteous and the sinners,

713
00:48:17,300 --> 00:48:20,306
 it contains the believers and the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

714
00:48:21,631 --> 00:48:24,845
And it's always going to be like that, until the day of judgment.

715
00:48:25,872 --> 00:48:31,203
But the ones, whom we should make sure that they are united

716
00:48:31,283 --> 00:48:36,124
and they are one and they are not disobeying Allahعَزّوجَلّ, are the Taifah Al-Mansourah(الطائفة المنصوره),

717
00:48:36,530 --> 00:48:40,201
this core group of Muslims, they are the ones who need to be united.

718
00:48:41,562 --> 00:48:45,487
Because their disobeying of Rasool Allah ﷺ, on that hill,

719
00:48:45,677 --> 00:48:49,002
was what brought defeat to the Muslims.

720
00:48:49,280 --> 00:48:54,687
It was the action of those 40 men on the mountain that brought defeat to the Muslims.

721
00:48:54,997 --> 00:48:58,400
It wasn't the 300 who left with Andullah Bin Obaey(عبدالله بن أبي)

722
00:48:59,173 --> 00:49:00,289
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

723
00:49:00,781 --> 00:49:08,046
وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ ۖ

724
00:49:08,353 --> 00:49:20,091
حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فَشِلْتُمْ وَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ وَعَصَيْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَرَاكُمْ مَا تُحِبُّونَ ۚ

725
00:49:20,671 --> 00:49:28,807
مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيَا وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ ۚ

726
00:49:29,133 --> 00:49:35,752
ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْ ۖ وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْ ۗ

727
00:49:36,054 --> 00:49:41,699
وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

728
00:49:42,182 --> 00:49:44,846
It was when, you disunited and you failed,

729
00:49:45,495 --> 00:49:49,600
and you disobeyed the messenger of Allah, that is when you lost.

730
00:49:50,934 --> 00:49:51,856
Next lesson,

731
00:49:52,211 --> 00:49:53,483
you know, you would expect that

732
00:49:53,578 --> 00:50:00,406
the sight of the mountain of Uhud(أحَد), would bring back bad memories to Rasool Allah ﷺ, sad memories,

733
00:50:01,077 --> 00:50:03,662
the defeat, in fact the first defeat of Muslims,

734
00:50:04,408 --> 00:50:11,474
the loss of Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبد المطلب), the dear uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ, loss of 70 Shahadaa(شهدآء),

735
00:50:12,158 --> 00:50:15,641
the injury of Rasool Allah ﷺ, so it's all bad memories

736
00:50:16,662 --> 00:50:18,458
but Rasool Allah ﷺ was optimistic.

737
00:50:19,321 --> 00:50:21,822
And he hated pessimism.

738
00:50:22,501 --> 00:50:24,165
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

739
00:50:24,434 --> 00:50:28,404
اُحَدْ جَبَلٌ يُحِبُّنَا وَنُحِبُّهُ

740
00:50:29,232 --> 00:50:33,280
Uhud(أحَد) is or a mountain that loves us, and we love it.

741
00:50:33,894 --> 00:50:38,322
So, this mountain rather than bringing sad memories,

742
00:50:38,433 --> 00:50:41,617
no, it's a mountain that loves us and we love it.

743
00:50:42,218 --> 00:50:43,373
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

744
00:50:43,413 --> 00:50:45,134
اُحَدْ جَبَلٌ فِيْ الْجَنَّةْ

745
00:50:45,174 --> 00:50:47,016
Uhud(أحَد) is a mountain in paradise.

746
00:50:47,998 --> 00:50:54,782
So, throw away pessimism, throw away associating the mountain of Uhud(أحَد) with sad memories,

747
00:50:54,862 --> 00:50:55,424
 No,

748
00:50:55,774 --> 00:51:00,202
whenever we see it, we will be we optimistic, whenever we see it, we will remember love.

749
00:51:00,732 --> 00:51:05,354
We're not going to remember defeat and hardship and pain we're going to remember love.

750
00:51:06,407 --> 00:51:08,919
This is a mountain that we love and it loves us.

751
00:51:09,855 --> 00:51:12,867
This is an important lesson that the Muslim should always look at the bright side,

752
00:51:12,931 --> 00:51:14,439
and the Muslims should always be optimistic.

753
00:51:16,025 --> 00:51:21,773
Next, the rules of victory and defeat in Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال) and Al-Imran (العمران).

754
00:51:22,661 --> 00:51:24,346
There are many rules of victory and defeat.

755
00:51:24,386 --> 00:51:27,607
But we'll stick to those mentioned in Al Imran(العمران) and Al-Anfaal(الانفال)

756
00:51:27,647 --> 00:51:31,110
because these are the two Sura's(سُوَر) revealed after Badr(بَدر) and Uhud(اُحَد)

757
00:51:31,135 --> 00:51:34,135
and these are the two battles that we have talked about.

758
00:51:34,737 --> 00:51:40,142
So, what are the rules of victory in Qur'an, specifically in Al-Imran(العمران) Al-Anfaal(الانفال).

759
00:51:40,273 --> 00:51:45,541
Number one, first and foremost, victory is from Allah.

760
00:51:45,863 --> 00:51:47,010
It belongs to Allah.

761
00:51:47,572 --> 00:51:48,898
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

762
00:51:49,045 --> 00:51:56,167
وَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشْرَىٰ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ بِهِ قُلُوبُكُمْ ۚ

763
00:51:56,532 --> 00:52:04,468
وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

764
00:52:04,618 --> 00:52:07,949
And victory is not but from Allah.

765
00:52:09,209 --> 00:52:10,697
verse 10 Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال).

766
00:52:11,223 --> 00:52:13,112
So it belongs to Him,

767
00:52:14,080 --> 00:52:18,411
It doesn't belong to your arms, it doesn't belong to your preparation.

768
00:52:18,840 --> 00:52:24,098
It doesn't belong to a particular King or leader, it belongs to Allah.

769
00:52:24,856 --> 00:52:28,217
Number two, if Allah wants to give you victory,

770
00:52:28,257 --> 00:52:33,331
no one, no power on earth can stop that from happening.

771
00:52:34,346 --> 00:52:35,737
So, you should fear no one.

772
00:52:36,126 --> 00:52:40,238
As long as Allah wants to hand you down His victory, it's going to happen.

773
00:52:40,695 --> 00:52:42,295
He gave it to Musa(موسى).

774
00:52:43,109 --> 00:52:45,542
When Musa(موسى) was fighting against Firaun(فرعون).

775
00:52:46,803 --> 00:52:48,262
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

776
00:52:48,659 --> 00:52:53,603
إِنْ يَنْصُرْكُمُ اللَّهُ فَلَا غَالِبَ لَكُمْ ۖ

777
00:52:53,841 --> 00:53:00,738
وَإِنْ يَخْذُلْكُمْ فَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَنْصُرُكُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ ۗ

778
00:53:00,984 --> 00:53:06,421
وَعَلَى اللَّهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ۝

779
00:53:07,394 --> 00:53:09,438
Verse 160 Al-Imran(العمران),

780
00:53:10,139 --> 00:53:13,948
if Allah should aid you no one can overcome you.

781
00:53:14,388 --> 00:53:16,228
But if He should forsake you,

782
00:53:16,540 --> 00:53:21,957
who is there that can aid you after Him and upon Allah, the believers rely.

783
00:53:22,478 --> 00:53:24,790
Rely on Allah because victory comes from Him.

784
00:53:25,251 --> 00:53:26,901
And don't rely on anybody else.

785
00:53:26,941 --> 00:53:29,766
Because if you rely on anybody else, Allah will forsake you.

786
00:53:30,501 --> 00:53:36,924
Number three, attachment to this world and preferring it over Aakhira(آخرة) is a reason for defeat.

787
00:53:37,748 --> 00:53:41,860
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said, and Allah has certainly fulfilled His promise to you,

788
00:53:41,899 --> 00:53:43,708
when you were killing them by His permission.

789
00:53:44,364 --> 00:53:46,836
This was the beginning of the battle of Uhud(أحَد), they were winning,

790
00:53:47,872 --> 00:53:55,122
وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ ۖ

791
00:53:55,415 --> 00:54:07,176
حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فَشِلْتُمْ وَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ وَعَصَيْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَرَاكُمْ مَا تُحِبُّونَ ۚ

792
00:54:07,703 --> 00:54:15,876
مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيَا وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ ۚ

793
00:54:16,160 --> 00:54:22,858
ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْ ۖ وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْ ۗ

794
00:54:23,080 --> 00:54:28,712
وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

795
00:54:29,263 --> 00:54:31,767
Until the time, when you lost courage,

796
00:54:32,077 --> 00:54:35,942
and fell to disputing about the order given by the prophet

797
00:54:36,164 --> 00:54:40,633
 and disobeyed him, after he had shown you that which you love,

798
00:54:40,881 --> 00:54:43,496
among you are some who desire this world.

799
00:54:44,926 --> 00:54:48,217
See, because of this desire of this world, you lost.

800
00:54:49,241 --> 00:54:53,021
Also a reason for losing, disobeying Rasool Allah ﷺ,

801
00:54:53,148 --> 00:54:56,299
another reason for losing is disunity

802
00:54:57,217 --> 00:55:02,828
and these are going to come up, obedience to Rasool Allah ﷺ in having unity.

803
00:55:03,475 --> 00:55:08,332
Number four, numbers are not the cause for victory or defeat.

804
00:55:08,914 --> 00:55:12,062
Lack of numbers doesn't bring defeat

805
00:55:12,475 --> 00:55:15,339
and overwhelming numbers do not bring victory.

806
00:55:15,379 --> 00:55:18,304
This is very important to learn, don't depend on your numbers.

807
00:55:18,800 --> 00:55:23,043
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said in Al-Imran(العمران), verse 123,

808
00:55:23,195 --> 00:55:29,341
وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنْتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ۖ

809
00:55:29,508 --> 00:55:33,706
فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ۝

810
00:55:33,981 --> 00:55:38,457
And already had Allah given you victory in the Battle of Badr(بدر), when you were weak.

811
00:55:38,825 --> 00:55:40,172
i.e. few in numbers.

812
00:55:40,819 --> 00:55:43,379
you were few numbers in Badr(بدر) and nevertheless, you won.

813
00:55:43,807 --> 00:55:47,319
While Allahعَزّوجَلّ say is about the Battle of Hunain(حنين).

814
00:55:47,756 --> 00:55:55,346
لَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ فِي مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيرَةٍ ۙ وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ

815
00:55:55,711 --> 00:56:03,836
وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ إِذْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا

816
00:56:04,101 --> 00:56:12,566
وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُمْ مُدْبِرِينَ۝

817
00:56:13,130 --> 00:56:16,566
And on the Day of Hunain(حنين), you were impressed by your numbers.

818
00:56:16,786 --> 00:56:18,825
And those numbers didn't do you any good,

819
00:56:18,850 --> 00:56:20,378
they lost the battle of Hunain(حنين).

820
00:56:21,047 --> 00:56:22,243
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

821
00:56:22,378 --> 00:56:27,665
And how many small parties have defeated larger parties by the will of Allah.

822
00:56:28,053 --> 00:56:30,938
This did not only happen with you Muhammadﷺ,

823
00:56:30,962 --> 00:56:33,354
it did happen with the righteous people before you,

824
00:56:34,139 --> 00:56:35,577
like the people of Talut(طالوت).

825
00:56:35,965 --> 00:56:37,821
They were small in numbers and they still won.

826
00:56:38,150 --> 00:56:41,778
So, numbers don't have anything to do with victory or defeat.

827
00:56:43,038 --> 00:56:43,893
Number five,

828
00:56:43,950 --> 00:56:46,699
obeying Allahعَزّوجَلّ and His Messenger and we talked about this,

829
00:56:46,960 --> 00:56:50,151
number six unity, unity is important.

830
00:56:50,796 --> 00:56:53,071
Number seven, perseverance.

831
00:56:53,333 --> 00:56:54,565
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

832
00:56:54,772 --> 00:57:02,686
وَأَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَلَا تَنَازَعُوا فَتَفْشَلُوا وَتَذْهَبَ رِيحُكُمْ ۖ

833
00:57:02,917 --> 00:57:08,559
وَاصْبِرُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ۝

834
00:57:08,830 --> 00:57:14,492
And obey Allah and His messenger and do not dispute and thus lose courage.

835
00:57:14,732 --> 00:57:18,252
And then your strength will depart and be patient.

836
00:57:18,371 --> 00:57:20,677
Be patient here it says Was-Biroo(واصبروا),

837
00:57:20,702 --> 00:57:23,912
we could say that that is either patience, or perseverance.

838
00:57:25,075 --> 00:57:26,835
Number eight, preparation.

839
00:57:27,066 --> 00:57:29,447
Be prepared but don't depend on preparation,

840
00:57:29,752 --> 00:57:33,047
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ telling you, be prepared physically,

841
00:57:33,363 --> 00:57:34,302
mentally,

842
00:57:34,669 --> 00:57:38,383
militarily in terms of arms training, you need to be prepared

843
00:57:38,750 --> 00:57:41,925
and prepare against them and this is in Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال) verse 60.

844
00:57:42,136 --> 00:57:55,488
وَأَعِدُّوا لَهُمْ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ قُوَّةٍ وَمِنْ رِبَاطِ الْخَيْلِ تُرْهِبُونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ وَعَدُوَّكُمْ

845
00:57:56,084 --> 00:58:04,788
وَآخَرِينَ مِنْ دُونِهِمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَهُمُ اللَّهُ يَعْلَمُهُمْ ۚ

846
00:58:05,122 --> 00:58:16,520
وَمَا تُنْفِقُوا مِنْ شَيْءٍ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ يُوَفَّ إِلَيْكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُونَ۝

847
00:58:16,957 --> 00:58:20,383
And prepare against them whatever you are able of power

848
00:58:20,533 --> 00:58:25,098
and of steals of war by which you may terrify the enemy of Allah

849
00:58:25,340 --> 00:58:28,271
and your enemy and others besides them,

850
00:58:28,442 --> 00:58:30,874
whom you do not know but whom Allah knows,

851
00:58:31,227 --> 00:58:34,907
and whatever you spend in the cause of Allah will be fully repaired to you

852
00:58:35,201 --> 00:58:36,793
and you will not be wronged.

853
00:58:37,321 --> 00:58:39,212
So, Muslims need to prepare.

854
00:58:39,719 --> 00:58:42,406
Number nine and number 10, steadfastness

855
00:58:42,834 --> 00:58:46,063
and then remembrance of Allah and these are mentioned in one Ayah(آية),

856
00:58:46,530 --> 00:58:48,015
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

857
00:58:48,698 --> 00:58:57,658
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا لَقِيتُمْ فِئَةً فَاثْبُتُوا

858
00:58:57,975 --> 00:59:03,399
وَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَثِيرًا لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ۝

859
00:59:03,565 --> 00:59:05,328
O you, who have believed,

860
00:59:05,592 --> 00:59:10,548
when you encounter a company from the enemy forces stand firm.

861
00:59:10,954 --> 00:59:15,651
And remember Allah much that you may be successful.

862
00:59:15,852 --> 00:59:17,767
So number one, stand firm.

863
00:59:18,030 --> 00:59:20,008
Don't move from that spot.

864
00:59:20,314 --> 00:59:22,164
Don't turn your back to the enemy.

865
00:59:22,378 --> 00:59:26,252
And remember Allah, Zikr(ذكر) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ all the time.

866
00:59:27,653 --> 00:59:29,997
الله اكبر، سبحان الله ،لا اله الا الله

867
00:59:30,257 --> 00:59:32,704
Connect that heart to Allahعَزّوجَلّ you will win.

868
00:59:33,042 --> 00:59:36,149
And this is verse 45, in Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال).

869
00:59:36,775 --> 00:59:38,318
And another verse, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

870
00:59:38,746 --> 00:59:40,667
and this is Surat Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال) verse 15;

871
00:59:40,830 --> 00:59:53,285
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا لَقِيتُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا زَحْفًا فَلَا تُوَلُّوهُمُ الْأَدْبَارَ۝

872
00:59:53,872 --> 00:59:59,020
O you, who have believed, when you meet those who disbelieved advancing for battle,

873
00:59:59,288 --> 01:00:01,803
 do not turn them your backs in fight,

874
01:00:02,114 --> 01:00:03,110
stand firm.

875
01:00:03,463 --> 01:00:04,662
وَثْبُتُوْ

876
01:00:05,467 --> 01:00:10,765
We'll carry on with some other lessons from the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) In Sha Allah ho Ta'ala(ان شاءالله تعالى) tomorrow night.

877
01:00:11,070 --> 01:00:15,988
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

878
01:00:16,253 --> 01:00:19,167
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

